# VAELEN - sitting S2 (19.06, build of the scene review's commit), 2026-09-27. 19.01, ADR-0159.
#
# Written BEFORE the log landed, as s1.session was: the owner builds the scene review's commit (its
# hash is `head` below, set by the commit after it, which is why the two differ by one), launches
# the walk mode (ENGINE_HANDOFF "sitting S2"), types `Vaelen.Walk 128 120`, and the whole
# Saved/Logs/Vaelen.log comes back with `git rev-parse HEAD` as its first line. Until the log is
# committed under the name below, no CTest entry names this file; Session.P19S2 is added with it.
#
# The twin is the Atlas begun THE WAY Vaelen.Walk BEGINS - Play and Stream, the climate on, the
# daily cadence (`--empty --stream`), which is not the world `--scene-terrain R` alone builds:
# measured on 2026-09-26, that world is one cold death from this one (1581 against 1582). Region
# 26 is where the played life of the 128/120 world stands at Begin (Run.Soak, the same wiring).
# In the raw log every line reads `LogVaelenWalk: LogVaelenScene: ...` - the engine's category,
# then the line's own; Tools/check_session.py reads from the last (19.11b).
log s2-2026-09-27.log
head 2234b2fcfab5dbf6ab48cbe5bad0d5930bfa70ef
run --empty --stream --climate --want-bound 0 --size 128 --years 120 --scene --scene-terrain 26
line LogVaelenScene: AELVOR 128 seed 41454c564f52 region 26:
line LogVaelenClimate: AELVOR 128
other --size 128 --prehistory 300 --years 120 --scene-terrain 26
